# Documentation Consolidation & Sync Strategy

This plan outlines how to move and organize all your research/brain files from the system-managed Gemini directory into your project, while maintaining their chronological and chat-based context.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **User Sovereignty**: This script is provided as a utility in your project. You own it and can change its logic anytime.
> 
> **Customization Points**: 
> - **Folder Naming**: Line 27-31 controls how folders are named (Date + Task Title).
> - **Filtering**: Line 40-45 controls which files are skipped (e.g., ignoring [.resolved](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d7e3ed05-2fb9-4b12-97a8-302ab75b8083/task.md.resolved) files).

## Proposed Changes

We will create a consolidation script that does the following:
1. Loops through each "Session" folder in your Brain directory.
2. Identifies the primary task or topic of that session (by reading [task.md](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/5e6e289c-3ada-49e0-b3ac-0f69997208eb/task.md)).
3. Copies all files (including [.resolved](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/d7e3ed05-2fb9-4b12-97a8-302ab75b8083/task.md.resolved) and [task.md](file:///C:/Users/Naween/.gemini/antigravity/brain/5e6e289c-3ada-49e0-b3ac-0f69997208eb/task.md)) into a structured folder in `apps/gurudevi-mobile/Docs v 3.0/brain_archive/`.

